They don't like to answer questions like that :) Certainly Pat Rankin,
who is a DevTeam member, posts here occasionally, though I haven't seen
one in a while; that could mean anything or nothing, though. I think that
"who are the DevTeam" is answerable: the end of the Guidebook tells you
who it was for 3.4, at least.

The bugs list continues to grow, and continues to mostly be
marked as either fixed (this branch) or Fixed (next major release):
http://nethack.org/v343/bugs.html Your guess is as good as mine if we will
ever see any of those fixes; for a while I could have told you exactly
when the bug list had last been updated, but I've long since given up on
that. Information on compiling with MS Visual Studio was posted on 10
Dec 2007, and there was an April Fools' joke this year, but other than
those and the buglist I don't think there's been any explicit activity.

My outsider's guess is that there's still earnest effort going into it
but there's no one making it their Serious Project to Get A New Version
Out, and when a game's been around for twenty years, there's not really
a rush. This might lead to a new version in another six months or years,
or it might not. Of course, for all I know, there's just one volunteer
updating the bugs list and choosing whether to write fixed or Fixed on
a whim; of course, for all I know, NetHack 4.0.0 will be released next
week and it will be a complete rewrite and an incredible game. The only
thing I know for sure is that you're not going to get an authoritative
answer asking about it on Usenet. :)

